ine v4.5.1\n\n### System information\n\nmacOS 26.0.1 (25A362) Godot Engine v4.6.dev2.official.7864ac801\n\n### Issue description\n\nI'm currently using JetBrains Rider (2025.2.4) with Godot v4.6.dev2, and when editing a file, the Godot console is filled with multiple lines of:\n```\nERROR: Bug: Dictionary::operator[] used when there was no value for the given key, please report.\n```\nNot sure if this is a LSP or Rider specific.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Open Godot 4.6.beta2, and create a basic project.\n2. Create a new GDScript file \"main.gd\".\n3. Open JetBrains Rider and open the Godot project\n4. make an edit to the file \"main.gd”.\n5. Switch back to Godot and observe the console messages. \n\nThis is assuming that Rider is able to connect to the LSP.\n\n\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n```GDScript\nextends Node3D\n\n# var message:String = \"Uncomment this line in Rider\"\n\n```\n","closed_by":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/iss